WEBVTT

00:00:01.560 --> 00:00:05.550
<i>This is what the general public thinks 
of the ideal bookstore employee.</i>

00:00:03.580 --> 00:00:07.590
Happy

00:00:04.250 --> 00:00:07.590
Cheerful

00:00:05.550 --> 00:00:07.590
Welcome!

00:00:05.720 --> 00:00:07.590
Perfect

00:00:07.780 --> 00:00:10.250
<i>But, in reality...</i>

00:00:10.950 --> 00:00:12.840
Welcome.

00:00:11.060 --> 00:00:12.690
Scary

00:00:11.520 --> 00:00:12.690
Scary

00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:14.590
That's bad. That's bad.

00:00:14.870 --> 00:00:16.000
What's up?

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:19.320
Honda's up next for that 
customer service coaching.

00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:22.600
Huh, you mean that notoriously 
over-enthusiastic one they do every year?

00:00:22.600 --> 00:00:23.220
Hey, now!

00:00:23.220 --> 00:00:26.650
Call it a "passionate coaching session 
for presenting an ideal image."

00:00:26.970 --> 00:00:32.270
Those who've received the coaching 
will be ranked by the instructors.

00:00:32.270 --> 00:00:33.370
Eternally.

00:00:32.480 --> 00:00:36.450
<b>Eternally</b>

00:00:33.370 --> 00:00:36.030
<i>That's an </i>eternally<i> useless ranking.</i>

00:00:36.760 --> 00:00:38.280
Okay, I'm off.

00:00:38.280 --> 00:00:40.090
I'm actually kind of interested.

00:00:40.090 --> 00:00:42.110
Fill me in later.

00:00:44.150 --> 00:00:47.890
<i>At the time, I was completely
 underestimating it.</i>

00:00:48.520 --> 00:00:53.580
<i>I had no idea that what awaited me 
was a terrifying coaching session</i>

00:00:53.580 --> 00:00:57.560
<i>that deeply alters the participants' minds.</i>

00:01:59.860 --> 00:02:02.900
<b>The Reception Training of Hell</b>

00:02:03.590 --> 00:02:05.830
<i>I just got here and I already want to go home.</i>

00:02:10.310 --> 00:02:11.240
<i>Pretty lady!</i>

00:02:11.240 --> 00:02:12.960
<i>Pretty lady at the entrance!</i>

00:02:19.610 --> 00:02:22.170
Hello!

00:02:22.170 --> 00:02:23.720
Are you here for the coaching?

00:02:23.720 --> 00:02:25.410
Yes, I am.

00:02:25.410 --> 00:02:28.280
Jeez, I'm so nervous.

00:02:28.280 --> 00:02:30.160
I know, right?

00:02:30.660 --> 00:02:34.090
<i>I have a surprisingly 
good feeling about this.</i>

00:02:32.430 --> 00:02:36.400
<b>A kind world</b>

00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:38.230
<b>Customer Service Coaching Venue</b>

00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:38.230
<b>Bam</b>

00:02:38.200 --> 00:02:40.470
<b>Rumble Rumble...</b>

00:02:41.030 --> 00:02:44.970
<b>The chosen sacrifices</b>

00:02:51.740 --> 00:02:54.410
Okay! Hello, everyone.

00:02:54.880 --> 00:02:59.710
My name is Hohoemi Bancho.
 I will be your instructor today.

00:02:59.710 --> 00:03:04.510
And this is the customer service expert, 
Assistant Manager Budda-head.

00:03:04.510 --> 00:03:06.020
Nice to meet you.

00:03:06.440 --> 00:03:07.860
<i>I hear it...</i>

00:03:08.570 --> 00:03:10.740
<i>It's the intro to Hell!</i>

00:03:11.230 --> 00:03:13.320
Let's get started.

00:03:13.780 --> 00:03:16.850
You there, in the front 
left seat, please come up.

00:03:17.580 --> 00:03:21.560
Let's start by sharing how you 
normally approach your customers.

00:03:25.030 --> 00:03:26.490
<i>Customer service training from Hell!</i>

00:03:26.740 --> 00:03:29.110
<i>And it's starting from the chorus!</i>

00:03:26.740 --> 00:03:29.550
<b>Customer Service Training from Hell 
Song/music: Hohoemi Bancho 
Arranged by: Assistant Manager Budda-head
 - intro -
 Chorus 1 
Chorus 2
 - Bridge - 
Second Chorus 1
 Second Chorus 2</b>

00:03:29.680 --> 00:03:30.620
Oh, dear!

00:03:30.620 --> 00:03:32.060
You can relax.

00:03:32.060 --> 00:03:32.670
Okay.

00:03:32.670 --> 00:03:35.500
That's a nice track suit, by the way.

00:03:33.690 --> 00:03:39.460
Volleyball Club

00:03:35.500 --> 00:03:37.200
Thank you.

00:03:37.200 --> 00:03:39.160
<i>It says Volleyball Club on it...</i>

00:03:39.640 --> 00:03:42.770
I understand that your usual customer service

00:03:40.790 --> 00:03:46.220
<b>Welcome, this—way—</b>

00:03:42.770 --> 00:03:46.080
is based on the role playing 
described by our company.

00:03:46.080 --> 00:03:47.460
"Welcome."

00:03:47.460 --> 00:03:49.190
"Just a moment, please."

00:03:49.190 --> 00:03:50.650
"Thank you for waiting."

00:03:50.650 --> 00:03:54.070
"Thank you, please come again."

00:03:54.070 --> 00:03:57.880
Today, we will be working to 
polish these basic phrases.

00:03:58.190 --> 00:04:01.920
Assistant Manager Buddha-head, may I ask 
you to play the part of the customer?

00:04:01.920 --> 00:04:02.760
Okay.

00:04:03.690 --> 00:04:05.960
Go ahead, Volleyball Club-san!

00:04:06.750 --> 00:04:07.560
W—

00:04:08.790 --> 00:04:09.680
W—

00:04:10.820 --> 00:04:11.450
W...

00:04:12.220 --> 00:04:13.850
Welcome!

00:04:13.850 --> 00:04:16.460
<i>Nervous breakdown!</i>

00:04:16.460 --> 00:04:19.330
Be true to yourself, Volleyball Club-san!

00:04:19.330 --> 00:04:20.860
Be natural!

00:04:20.860 --> 00:04:21.400
Go ahead!

00:04:21.400 --> 00:04:23.350
O-One moment, please.

00:04:23.350 --> 00:04:24.440
Smile!

00:04:24.440 --> 00:04:26.490
If you could wait just a second, please.

00:04:26.490 --> 00:04:27.980
Look your customer in the eye.

00:04:27.980 --> 00:04:29.410
Thank you very much.

00:04:29.600 --> 00:04:31.630
Don't glare at them!

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:33.720
<i>What a...</i>

00:04:34.250 --> 00:04:37.260
<i>What a merciless public execution!</i>

00:04:39.030 --> 00:04:41.190
Did I make you a bit nervous?

00:04:41.190 --> 00:04:44.630
Assistant Manager Buddha-head, 
could you please demonstrate?

00:04:44.630 --> 00:04:45.520
Sure.

00:04:48.760 --> 00:04:50.040
Welcome!

00:04:50.040 --> 00:04:52.170
May I put a cover on it?

00:04:52.390 --> 00:04:53.920
Thank you for waiting.

00:04:53.920 --> 00:04:55.400
Thank you very much.

00:04:55.400 --> 00:04:57.600
Please come again.

00:04:58.400 --> 00:05:00.400
<i>But he was like a demon!</i>

00:05:00.400 --> 00:05:02.840
<i>He was like a demon!</i>

00:05:02.840 --> 00:05:05.700
Thank you very much, Assistant 
Manager Buddha-head.

00:05:06.170 --> 00:05:07.910
<i>He's a little too in-control.</i>

00:05:08.180 --> 00:05:14.980
With the Assistant Manager's role playing, 
we were able to review something important.

00:05:15.120 --> 00:05:17.820
That's right, a smile is a muscle!

00:05:17.820 --> 00:05:19.590
<i>I've never heard this!</i>

00:05:19.750 --> 00:05:23.270
A customer service smile can 
only be made through training.

00:05:22.200 --> 00:05:23.900
Welcome.

00:05:23.270 --> 00:05:27.760
A welcoming attitude is built on
 a smile, which is based on muscles.

00:05:28.310 --> 00:05:30.460
Please stand, everyone.

00:05:30.700 --> 00:05:33.870
First and third rows, face right.

00:05:35.440 --> 00:05:36.650
H-Hi.

00:05:37.200 --> 00:05:38.190
Hi.

00:05:38.470 --> 00:05:42.390
Please make certain you are
 smiling, no other expressions.

00:05:42.390 --> 00:05:45.850
First, we'll have you form pairs of two.

00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:49.350
If you find your partner's smile inadequate,

00:05:49.350 --> 00:05:51.480
be sure to point it out honestly.

00:05:51.830 --> 00:05:54.280
On my signal, say, "Welcome!"

00:05:54.280 --> 00:05:58.560
and keep your best smile 
until my next signal.

00:05:58.560 --> 00:06:00.180
Are you ready?

00:06:00.180 --> 00:06:02.230
Here we go!

00:06:02.230 --> 00:06:03.470
Welcome!

00:06:03.470 --> 00:06:05.000
Okay, keep it there.

00:06:05.000 --> 00:06:07.430
That's right. Notice your muscles.

00:06:07.430 --> 00:06:09.370
That's a <i>little</i> too much, 
Volleyball Club-san.

00:06:09.370 --> 00:06:11.670
But your attitude is great!

00:06:11.670 --> 00:06:13.280
Keep your smiles!

00:06:13.280 --> 00:06:16.640
You're not there yet! You still aren't
 feeling welcoming enough!

00:06:16.830 --> 00:06:17.880
Thank you!

00:06:17.880 --> 00:06:19.880
Thank you for coming to our store!

00:06:20.270 --> 00:06:22.960
Now, remember to check your partner's smile.

00:06:22.960 --> 00:06:24.980
<i>Right, I totally forgot.</i>

00:06:25.240 --> 00:06:27.450
<i>He's not doing jack!</i>

00:06:27.640 --> 00:06:31.050
I think you could relax your shoulders a bit.

00:06:31.050 --> 00:06:32.090
Oh, right.

00:06:32.090 --> 00:06:33.090
Sorry.

00:06:33.090 --> 00:06:35.780
Okay, everyone, stop.

00:06:36.420 --> 00:06:39.600
Honda-san from the Tokyo branch, correct?

00:06:39.600 --> 00:06:40.110
Yes.

00:06:40.110 --> 00:06:42.450
You seemed to have received 
some advice just now.

00:06:42.450 --> 00:06:43.810
Do you think you can use it?

00:06:43.880 --> 00:06:45.550
Yes, indeed, totally!

00:06:46.170 --> 00:06:47.770
That's great.

00:06:47.770 --> 00:06:51.180
Okay, with that in mind, shall we try again?

00:06:51.610 --> 00:06:52.740
Ready, go!

00:06:52.740 --> 00:06:53.630
Welcome!

00:06:53.630 --> 00:06:54.440
Smile!

00:06:54.440 --> 00:06:55.180
Welcome!

00:06:55.180 --> 00:06:56.450
Don't hold back!

00:06:56.450 --> 00:06:59.980
Welcome! Welcome! Welcome!

00:06:57.930 --> 00:06:59.980
<i>What the hell was my job again?</i>

00:06:59.150 --> 00:06:59.980
<b>*He's a bookseller</b>

00:06:59.980 --> 00:07:00.880
It's opening!

00:07:00.880 --> 00:07:03.350
I can feel this part popping open!

00:07:03.350 --> 00:07:04.960
Well done.

00:07:07.230 --> 00:07:13.030
<i>I never knew smiling was so arduous.</i>

00:07:13.030 --> 00:07:16.950
You're doing very well. Perfect.

00:07:16.950 --> 00:07:19.260
Thank you.

00:07:19.270 --> 00:07:22.170
<i>Some people have no trouble at all.</i>

00:07:22.170 --> 00:07:23.470
Now, you, too.

00:07:23.470 --> 00:07:26.350
Take note of what she does well.

00:07:26.350 --> 00:07:27.240
Okay.

00:07:27.540 --> 00:07:29.280
It's her!

00:07:29.280 --> 00:07:31.230
The pretty lady at the entrance!

00:07:31.230 --> 00:07:34.620
Oh, wow, she was paired up 
with the assistant manager.

00:07:34.620 --> 00:07:35.890
Ready, go.

00:07:35.890 --> 00:07:37.220
Welcome.

00:07:35.890 --> 00:07:37.690
<b>Smürl</b>

00:07:37.690 --> 00:07:39.540
That's it. Keep it up.

00:07:39.540 --> 00:07:40.990
How about some vocal practice?

00:07:41.470 --> 00:07:43.740
Smile into the heavens from 
your forehead, and shout.

00:07:47.560 --> 00:07:50.320
Now, let's try smiling without shouting.

00:07:50.320 --> 00:07:51.500
Now, smile!

00:07:51.530 --> 00:07:53.070
<b>Grõnk</b>

00:07:53.250 --> 00:07:56.040
<i>Sh-She's ironclad!</i>

00:07:56.040 --> 00:07:58.360
<i>The badness of it... bravo!</i>

00:07:58.360 --> 00:08:01.390
<i>It's not like she has a 
belligerent, lazy attitude.</i>

00:08:01.390 --> 00:08:04.620
<i>She's using her time here seriously.</i>

00:08:04.620 --> 00:08:05.430
<i>Probably.</i>

00:08:05.430 --> 00:08:06.060
<i>I think.</i>

00:08:06.060 --> 00:08:07.010
<i>Maybe.</i>

00:08:07.010 --> 00:08:11.910
<i>But, like, I don't know how I'm 
supposed to feel about any of this.</i>

00:08:12.350 --> 00:08:13.940
That's it, that's great!

00:08:13.940 --> 00:08:16.060
<i>Oh no, it's two-on-one!</i>

00:08:16.060 --> 00:08:19.720
I really appreciate your 
sentiment of thankfulness.

00:08:19.720 --> 00:08:21.590
Let's try making an "oo" 
and "ee" sound together.

00:08:21.590 --> 00:08:23.350
Relax your face.

00:08:26.360 --> 00:08:27.770
<i>Of course.</i>

00:08:28.450 --> 00:08:31.680
<i>The pretty lady has nice teeth, too.</i>

00:08:29.640 --> 00:08:32.710
<b>Distracting himself from reality</b>

00:08:33.480 --> 00:08:34.610
Now, then...

00:08:34.840 --> 00:08:37.680
We're already out of time.

00:08:37.890 --> 00:08:40.130
A final word, Assistant Manager.

00:08:40.130 --> 00:08:41.150
Right.

00:08:42.090 --> 00:08:46.850
Shoplifters and undesirable customers tend 
not to like smiles and upbeat energy.

00:08:47.020 --> 00:08:49.660
Your smiles can be mastered 
and put to good use.

00:08:49.660 --> 00:08:54.590
Please remember today's 
training in your daily work.

00:08:54.700 --> 00:08:57.400
Thank you for your time today.

00:08:57.400 --> 00:08:59.600
Thank you.

00:09:01.360 --> 00:09:03.820
<i>I can't believe how tired I am.</i>

00:09:03.820 --> 00:09:05.590
Goodbye, now.

00:09:08.550 --> 00:09:10.180
Good work today.

00:09:13.960 --> 00:09:16.480
<i>That was a normal smile.</i>

00:09:16.480 --> 00:09:18.740
<i>Finally seeing the pretty lady smile</i>

00:09:18.740 --> 00:09:24.260
<i>brought just a little bit of peace 
to my soul after a day of torment.</i>

00:09:25.990 --> 00:09:28.990
<b>Mission: An Outside Work-ish Job</b>

00:09:29.140 --> 00:09:32.650
<i>Okitsune-senpai was chosen 
to go to the next coaching.</i>

00:09:34.750 --> 00:09:37.280
I don't want to go!

00:09:37.280 --> 00:09:38.510
The death voice of her soul...

00:09:38.570 --> 00:09:40.550
That was a voice from Hell.

00:09:40.550 --> 00:09:42.280
I've never even been to this place.

00:09:42.280 --> 00:09:43.550
Why the heck is it here?

00:09:43.550 --> 00:09:44.790
Where is this place?

00:09:44.790 --> 00:09:46.480
I guess you'll know when you get there.

00:09:46.480 --> 00:09:49.240
I don't deal well with this crap, Honda.

00:09:49.240 --> 00:09:51.910
Dammit, this is such a pain in the ass.

00:09:51.910 --> 00:09:54.960
But getting lost there is even worse, so...

00:09:55.190 --> 00:09:56.970
I'll go ask Fullface.

00:09:56.970 --> 00:09:58.550
He's good at this stuff.

00:09:58.550 --> 00:10:01.100
<i>Why did you ask me first, then?</i>

00:10:01.430 --> 00:10:02.460
<b>10 minutes later</b>

00:10:01.430 --> 00:10:02.460
10 minutes later...

00:10:02.720 --> 00:10:04.560
I knew I could trust Fullface.

00:10:04.560 --> 00:10:07.650
He gave me some really easy directions.

00:10:08.140 --> 00:10:09.530
What a pain.

00:10:09.530 --> 00:10:11.430
Guess I'll check it out 
on my way home today.

00:10:11.740 --> 00:10:13.070
<b>The next day</b>

00:10:11.740 --> 00:10:13.070
The next day...

00:10:13.270 --> 00:10:15.390
Man, the trains are packed.

00:10:15.390 --> 00:10:16.970
I'm gonna leave early.

00:10:17.340 --> 00:10:18.720
Ugh, this sucks.

00:10:18.720 --> 00:10:20.650
Guess I'll just smile all day.

00:10:20.650 --> 00:10:21.630
I'm off.

00:10:21.630 --> 00:10:23.140
See you.

00:10:24.680 --> 00:10:28.980
That girl's got a bad mouth, but she 
has a really good attitude, actually.
